      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "The way VRChat sees it is that 2fa is required, and you have a choice between email codes and authenticators. When they implemented this their explaination was that there was too high of a load on their support staff due to compromised accounts. I can kinda understand, VRChat is 11 years old and not everyone plays for that long, and older accounts will have a higher chance of password reuse.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-02-13T23:04:02.683Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I don’t understand why this is enforced for all users, especially when there is already a separate two-factor authentication (2FA) option that users can choose to enable or disable.\n\nIf users have the ability to opt into 2FA for additional security, it doesn’t make sense that one-time code verification via email is still mandatory for everyone, regardless of their preference. This lack of choice is frustrating, as it forces an extra step on users who may not need or want it.",
